---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../data/site';

const effective = 'October 25, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} collects, uses and protects information from visitors, newsletter subscribers and supporters.`}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-display font-bold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 mb-10">Effective {effective}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-a:text-mars-red hover:prose-a:text-mars-rust">
      <p>
        This policy explains what information {SITE_NAME} ("we", "us") collects when you use
        populationmars.com and orbitfleet.populationmars.com (the "sites"), why we collect it, and the
        choices you have. We collect as little as we can and we do not sell personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <h3>Information you give us</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Newsletter signups:</strong> your email address and the page you signed up from.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact and directory forms:</strong> your name, email address, organization, the topic you choose and your message. Directory submissions also include the company details you provide.</li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> anything you send to {SITE_EMAIL}.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Payments</h3>
      <p>
        Donations are processed by Stripe on Stripe-hosted checkout pages. We never see or store your
        full card number. Stripe shares with us the information needed to record the payment, such as
        your name, email address, amount and date. Stripe's handling of your data is described in the
        <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages are read and how visitors find us. It uses
        cookies and collects information such as pages viewed, approximate location derived from your IP
        address, device and browser type, and referring site. We use this only in aggregate. You can opt
        out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>
        or by blocking cookies in your browser. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses data from sites that use its services</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Hosting and simulator sessions</h3>
      <p>
        Our hosting providers keep standard server logs (IP address, request time, requested URL and
        browser user agent) for security and reliability. When you launch an OrbitFleet simulation, the
        service creates a short-lived session identifier so it can stream your simulation and limit
        concurrent use. Simulation sessions contain synthetic data only.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To send the newsletter you asked for.</li>
        <li>To reply to your messages and evaluate directory submissions.</li>
        <li>To process donations, send receipts and meet tax and accounting obligations.</li>
        <li>To keep the sites secure and understand how they are used.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share information only with service providers that run the sites for us: our hosting and
        form-handling provider (Netlify), Stripe for payments, and Google for analytics. We may disclose
        information if required by law. We do not sell or rent personal information, and we do not share
        it for cross-context behavioral advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Newsletter addresses are kept until you unsubscribe. Messages and form submissions are kept as
        long as needed to handle the conversation and for up to two years after. Payment records are
        kept as long as tax and accounting law requires.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time by replying "unsubscribe" or writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>. Depending on where you live, including the
        European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and California, you may have the right to access,
        correct, delete or receive a copy of your personal information, and to object to or restrict
        certain processing. To make a request, email us; we will respond within 30 days. You also have
        the right to complain to your local data-protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The sites are written for a general audience and are not directed at children under 13. We do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has sent us
        personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Our service providers may process information in the United States and other countries. Where
        required, they rely on recognized transfer mechanisms such as standard contractual clauses.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we will update the effective date above, and for material changes we
        will note it on the site or in the newsletter.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
